{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789913712,"nonce":"vsxbXIMQ/01MEkFyvupZE5mErdY=","title":"Lua: beat LuaJIT on every benchmark, correctness kept","message":"Baseline (2026-09-20, LLVM release, tiered, 3 interleaved rounds, medians): zylua beats LuaJIT on branchy alone and trails PUC Lua 5.4 on twelve of seventeen kernels. Worst: op_overload 12.6 s vs LuaJIT 13.6 ms, nbody 9.9 s vs 63 ms, method_call 1.06 s vs 5 ms, collatz 3.8 s vs 181 ms, mandelbrot 2.75 s vs 188 ms.\n\nCauses, from ZYNTAX_TRACE_GC and the kernels' shapes: the lattice has no Number (join(Int, Float) = Any, so mixed arithmetic boxes), no Func (a function held in a variable is Any and every call through it is dynamic), and no table shapes (every field is a boxed value in a dict, every method call a metatable walk). Short-lived tables allocate per iteration where LuaJIT sinks them.\n\nThe plan is the child issues, in order: Number, Func, shaped tables, scalar replacement of non-escaping shapes, start-up. Every step is measured with crates/zyntax_lua/benchmarks/run.py (medians and spread, never a single run) and gated on the conformance suite.","files":null}]}